From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 02:05:29 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Reuse the main pass's collision boxes for the step-up trial

Entity.move runs World.getCubes twice for a mob that can step up, over two boxes that
overlap almost completely: the step-up box sweeps the same x and z as the main pass, its
floor is the pre-move box's floor where the main pass's floor is that minus whatever
downward motion was asked for, and it only reaches higher. So the only blocks the second
scan can find that the first did not are the rows between the two ceilings.

Boxes the main pass collected outside the step-up box cannot clamp anything it does: the
offset helpers test overlap on the two axes they are not moving along, strictly, and every
candidate the trial builds stays inside its own swept volume. That is the same argument
vanilla relies on to scan a swept box at all. So the main pass's boxes can be kept and
only the rows above its ceiling collected, instead of reading the blocks under the entity
a second time.

Under the axis-by-axis scan the sink holds one axis' worth of boxes rather than the whole
swept volume, so there is nothing to reuse and the full scan stands.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/Entity.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/Entity.java
index 0d03516914051ff5076a0a9b25099907fd50e0f2..d8703e257f5e188d599c7fba6f86599d9c83d128 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/Entity.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/Entity.java
@@ -632,11 +632,38 @@ public abstract class Entity implements ICommandListener {
 
                 this.setEntityBoundingBox(preMinX, preMinY, preMinZ, preMaxX, preMaxY, preMaxZ);
                 d1 = (double) this.stepHeight;
-                // Athena - the step-up scan stacks on top of the main pass's boxes in the same sink
-                int stepMark = sink.mark();
-                this.world.getCubes(this,
-                        this.boundingBoxMinX + Math.min(d6, 0.0D), this.boundingBoxMinY + Math.min(d1, 0.0D), this.boundingBoxMinZ + Math.min(d8, 0.0D),
-                        this.boundingBoxMaxX + Math.max(d6, 0.0D), this.boundingBoxMaxY + Math.max(d1, 0.0D), this.boundingBoxMaxZ + Math.max(d8, 0.0D), sink);
+                // Athena start - the step-up scan stacks on top of the main pass's boxes in the same
+                // sink, and where it can it reuses them instead of collecting them again.
+                //
+                // The step-up box sweeps the same x and z as the main pass did, starts no lower
+                // (stepHeight is positive, so its floor is the pre-move box's floor, and the main
+                // pass's floor was that minus whatever downward motion was asked for), and only
+                // reaches higher. So the blocks it would find that the main pass did not are exactly
+                // the rows between the two ceilings. Boxes the main pass collected outside the
+                // step-up box cannot clamp anything: the offset helpers test overlap on the two axes
+                // they are not moving along, strictly, and every candidate the step-up trial builds
+                // stays inside its own swept volume.
+                //
+                // Under the axis-by-axis scan the sink holds one axis' worth of boxes rather than
+                // the whole swept volume, so there is nothing to reuse and the full scan stands.
+                double stepMinX = this.boundingBoxMinX + Math.min(d6, 0.0D);
+                double stepMinZ = this.boundingBoxMinZ + Math.min(d8, 0.0D);
+                double stepMaxX = this.boundingBoxMaxX + Math.max(d6, 0.0D);
+                double stepMaxZ = this.boundingBoxMaxZ + Math.max(d8, 0.0D);
+                double stepMaxY = this.boundingBoxMaxY + d1;
+                int stepMark;
+
+                if (axisScan) {
+                    stepMark = sink.mark();
+                    this.world.getCubes(this, stepMinX, this.boundingBoxMinY, stepMinZ, stepMaxX, stepMaxY, stepMaxZ, sink);
+                } else {
+                    stepMark = sinkMark;
+
+                    if (stepMaxY > totalMaxY) {
+                        this.world.getCubes(this, stepMinX, totalMaxY, stepMinZ, stepMaxX, stepMaxY, stepMaxZ, sink);
+                    }
+                }
+                // Athena end
 
                 // candidate A (was axisalignedbb4), starting from the current box
                 double aMinX = this.boundingBoxMinX, aMinY = this.boundingBoxMinY, aMinZ = this.boundingBoxMinZ;
